('CIT_SAINT_BERNARD_GOLDEN','ENT_SAINT_BERNARD','SRC_GOLDEN_LEGEND','The Golden Legend (Caxton)','The Golden Legend (Caxton)','James the More 104 THE GOLDEN LEGEND Bernard, a man of the bishopric of Mutina, as Calixtus the pope saith, was taken and enchained and put into a deep tower, and called always the blessed S. James, so that S. James appeared to him and said: Come and follow me into Galicia, and then his bonds brake and S. James vanished away.','William Caxton',1483,'https://archive.org/details/TheGoldenLegendV1',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'OCR scan of Caxtons Golden Legend, located by name; verify the saint.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
